cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CBCTScope: a local-first CBCT and 2D radiograph viewer with native AI-agent control"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Motaghi
    given-names: Reza
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3194-1879"
    website: "https://rezamotaghi.com"
abstract: >-
  CBCTScope is a free, open-source, local-first viewer for cone-beam CT volumes
  and 2D radiographs (panoramic, intraoral, CR, DX), built by a board-certified
  oral and maxillofacial radiologist. It reads uncompressed DICOM exports in
  place, with eight purpose-built reading modes: orthogonal MPR with 3D
  rendering, multi-slice grid, curved panoramic reconstruction with nerve
  tracing, TMJ with axis-corrected sections, freehand reslice, virtual
  cephalogram, region growing with airway analysis, and two-volume stitching.
  Scans never leave the user's computer: the server binds to loopback, nothing
  is uploaded, and no hosted instance exists. To our knowledge it is also the
  first CBCT viewer with native AI-agent control: a built-in Model Context
  Protocol (MCP) server exposes eight navigation-only verbs (open, mode,
  window, slice, snapshot, reset), so an agent can operate the viewer while
  producing no findings; interpretation remains with the human reader.
  Research use only; not a medical device.
repository-code: "https://github.com/rezamotaghi/cbctscope"
